WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.690
Two villages share one hillside
in the highlands of western Kenya.

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.850
Malaria spreads through the bites of some
infected female Anopheles mosquitoes.

3
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:15.250
In 2024 there were an estimated
282 million cases worldwide,

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.830
and 610,000 deaths.

5
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.630
Warmth matters too.

6
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:25.990
One model predicts the best conditions
for transmission at 25 degrees Celsius.

7
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.570
Yet one village has far
more malaria than the other.

8
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.150
Is it higher up the slope?

9
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.070
Or is it pure chance?

10
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.510
In this mission, you'll
link climate, landscape,

11
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.610
air and water to the
diseases people catch.

12
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.030
Then you'll weigh two global
killers: polluted air,

13
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.110
and water contaminated with faeces.

14
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.150
Your mission: explain why one village
might have far more malaria than the other.
